=== PRECONDITION REPAIR: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (merge=union multi-root corruption) ===
The committed apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was a .gitattributes
merge=union artifact with TWO <Project> roots (lines 1-1398 and 1399-2689) and an unbalanced
<ItemGroup>, so it failed XML load with:
  MSB4025: The project file could not be loaded. The 'ItemGroup' start tag on line 151 ...
This blocked ALL build/test at HEAD (verified: git working tree clean; HEAD itself carries 2 roots).
Repaired per the file's own documented invariant (and matching sibling logs 0073 SmallMultiplesChart,
0185 MapTileLayer): regenerated to ONE Project root with a single case-insensitive ordinal
path-sorted, Include-deduplicated Compile item group. The list is the union of both roots'
Compile links (root1: 1243 distinct, root2: 1230 distinct; union: 1246) — merge=union only ever
concatenates, so the union is the complete historical superset, 0 stale (every Include verified to
exist on disk) — plus the one new UptimeHeatmap.Model.cs link. Final: 1247 distinct Compile entries,
0 duplicates, single root, balanced ItemGroups, XML loads OK.

=== SURFACE DELIVERED (parity with web/src/components/status/UptimeHeatmap.tsx) ===
- 2-file native pattern (pure-presentational, like sibling ScoreBadge): UptimeHeatmap.Model.cs
  (WinUI-free projection, unit-tested) + UptimeHeatmap.cs (WinUI view, exercised by the app build).
  Shipped LOC: UptimeHeatmap.cs = 173, UptimeHeatmap.Model.cs = 323, UptimeHeatmapTests.cs = 354.
  A complete native port, not a skeleton/stub.
- Data: the web component is purely presentational (UptimeHeatmapProps: days/title/footnote) — its
  parent owns any fetching — so there is NO data hook and, exactly as the controlled web source has,
  NO loading/error/stale/offline fetch branch to reproduce (same rationale as siblings 0063
  AnnotationList / 0073 SmallMultiplesChart). The model reuses the shared P1/S8-adjacent Core types
  UptimeDay / HealthStatus / StatusPresentation (TeslaSync.App.Core.Status). The view performs no HTTP.
- States rendered (every branch the web source has — all unit-tested headlessly):
    * POPULATED  -> one VariableSizedWrapGrid square per day, oldest first, tinted by the shared
      status palette (StatusPresentation.AccentHex — the native counterpart of the web SQUARE_BG map),
      each with a date+status(+summary) tooltip and a "{date}: {label}" Narrator name; plus the rolling
      uptime caption "{fmtPercent(pct,2)} uptime" coloured by the web tiers (>=99 green / >=95 amber /
      else red); healthy + maintenance days count as up (StatusPresentation.UptimePercent).
    * EMPTY (no days) -> friendly TsEmptyState ("No status history yet"), never a blank box (the web
      renders an empty squares row; the native surface upgrades that per the P2 "never a blank box" rule).
- Shared components mapped to native counterparts (no raw web primitives, no direct chart-lib imports):
  web GlassPanel -> TsGlassPanel; web Tooltip -> WinUI ToolTipService; empty -> TsEmptyState;
  flex-wrap squares -> VariableSizedWrapGrid (the codebase's wrapping idiom); PanelTitle/Caption
  typography roles; status palette via DisplayPrimitives.HexBrush.
- i18n (P1/S10): every label resolves through ILocalizer with a minted translation.* key + a verbatim
  English fallback (the web inlines English with no t() calls; this is the ScoreBadge/ServiceStatus
  precedent — keys are NOT added to Strings/en/Resources.resw, the fallback resolves until a future
  i18n pass): status.uptime.title ("Uptime — last {{count}} days"), status.uptime.caption
  ("{{percent}} uptime"), status.uptime.listLabel ("Daily status history"), status.uptime.empty
  ("No status history yet"), status.label.{operational|degraded|outage|unknown|maintenance}. A
  RecordingLocalizer test asserts every key is requested. No hardcoded English literal in the surface.
- Accessibility: each day square carries its "{date}: {status}" name (web aria-label parity); the
  squares container carries the "Daily status history" list label (web role="list" aria-label); the
  whole surface carries heading + uptime caption as its automation name; FrameworkElementAutomationPeer.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened slug=UptimeHeatmap via UptimeHeatmapDiagnostics, fired once on Loaded.
  PII-safe — never logs the day window or the uptime value (asserted by a dedicated test).
- No TODO / FIXME / stub / mock / placeholder / Lorem / NotImplementedException in any shipped file.

